WEBVTT

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:10.596
Training gets new hires up to speed, and keeps everyone’s food handler cards in date. In this video, you’ll assign a course, sign off a step, and check who needs what.

00:00:11.667 --> 00:00:24.275
Open Training, then Courses. A course is a list of steps: lessons to read, quizzes with a pass mark, and sign-offs by a manager. Add the new hire course gives you a ready-made one to start from.

00:00:24.733 --> 00:00:30.493
To assign one, click Assign, pick the people, and how many days they have. Each person is told.

00:00:31.267 --> 00:00:38.264
Trainees work down the steps. In a quiz, they see what was right and why after each try, and the best score is kept.

00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:49.359
A sign-off is for something a manager has to see. Watch Lena open her station, then click Sign off. Trainees can’t tick their own, and AI can’t sign anything off.

00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:59.285
Team is where managers keep up: expired cards, overdue courses, missing cards, and sign-offs waiting. Needs attention lists who to chase first.

00:01:00.067 --> 00:01:10.115
Certifications lists the cards your company tracks, how long each lasts, and when to warn. An expired food handler card stops a shift being planned for that person.

00:01:10.567 --> 00:01:19.612
Anyone can add their own card, or tell Assist when it expires, and a manager verifies it. Expiring cards also show in the daily brief.
